//? Title: YOLACT shared prototypes and Fast NMS
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Separating objects into individual masks can be costly when each region needs its own feature crop. YOLACT predicts shared image-wide prototype maps and per-object coefficients. This report checks their tensor derivatives and Fast NMS,then visibly fits the complete compact model and inspects its actual held-out masks and learned basis.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/yolact.cpp`.

> The method

Shared prototype maps combine linearly with signed per-anchor coefficients. Box crops isolate each object's mask. Five shared prediction scales and a semantic auxiliary objective train jointly through explicit tensor Adam;Fast NMS uses every higher-scored predecessor.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/yolact_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/yolact_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/yolact_concept.tikz > build/yolact_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/yolact_concept.svg build/yolact_concept.dvi > build/yolact_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
