> A signed shared basis and per-object coefficients

YOLACT separates mask prediction into image-wide prototype maps and per-anchor
coefficients. If a pixel's K prototype values are \(p_{uvk}\),then object i
has logits

$$z_{iuv}=\sum_{k=1}^K p_{uvk}c_{ik},\qquad M_{iuv}=\sigma(z_{iuv})\mathbf1[(u,v)\text{ is inside its box}].$$
\alttext(Each instance combines shared prototypes with its own signed coefficients,then applies sigmoid and a box crop.)

Prototypes are ReLU maps and coefficients use tanh,so signed coefficients can
add or subtract image structure. Cropped mask BCE divides each instance's
summed pixel loss by its discrete crop area,floored at one,and then averages
instances. It does not divide by the whole image area. For a cropped pixel,
the prototype derivative is \((\sigma(z)-t)c_k/A\),and a coefficient derivative
sums \((\sigma(z)-t)p_k/A\) over the crop. Outside-crop derivatives are zero.
The following hand-check has two basis maps,six pixels and three cropped pixels;
native tests independently verify every logit,prototype/coefficient derivative,
zero-area crop and empty positive set.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/yolact_linear.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  auto proto = n::tensor({1., 2., -1., 3., 2., -2., 4., 1., 0., 2., -3., 1.}, {1, 2, 3, 2})
                   .requires_grad_(),
       coeff = n::tensor({.5, -.25}, {1, 2}).requires_grad_();
  const auto logits = m::LinearInstanceMasks(proto, coeff);
  const auto target = n::tensor({0., 1., 0., 1., 0., 1.}, {1, 2, 3}),
             crop = n::tensor({1., 1., 0., 0., 1., 0.}, {1, 2, 3});
  const auto loss = m::CroppedInstanceMaskLoss(logits, target, crop);
  const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, {proto, coeff});
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(logits.reshape({2, 3}), {0}), -2, 2),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(
           n::reverse(n::sum(n::abs(gradient[0]), {3}).reshape({2, 3}), {0}), 0, .3);
  a.title("Signed prototype mask logits");
  b.title("Prototype gradient magnitude");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/yolact_linear.svg");
  std::print("Three cropped pixels,area-normalized BCE {:.9f};coefficient derivatives "
             "{:.9f}/{:.9f}. Shared map values may be signed in this arithmetic fixture;the "
             "model prototypes use ReLU. No fitting.\n",
             loss.item(), gradient[1].to_vector<float>()[0],
             gradient[1].to_vector<float>()[1]);
}
```
