> Fast NMS includes suppressed predecessors

For scores sorted high to low,Fast NMS keeps candidate j only if
\(\max_{i<j}\operatorname{IoU}(b_i,b_j)\le\tau\). It compares every earlier
candidate,including candidates already suppressed. Greedy NMS compares only
kept predecessors. In this chain,A overlaps B and B overlaps C above.3,while
A overlaps C below.3. Fast NMS therefore keeps only A;greedy NMS keeps A and C.
Sorting is stable;images and categories are isolated,and the final cap resets
per image. Host maps group integer IDs only;score order,IoU,triangular masking
and selection all use tensors. Fast NMS is a different rule,not an exact
acceleration of greedy NMS.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/yolact_fast_nms.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  m::TensorDetections d{
      n::tensor({0., 0., 10., 10., 0., 4., 10., 14., 0., 8., 10., 18.}, {3, 4}),
      n::tensor({.9, .8, .7}), n::zeros({3}, n::DType::Int64), n::zeros({3}, n::DType::Int64)};
  const auto fast = m::TensorFastNms(d, .3),
             greedy = n::non_max_suppression(d.boxes, d.scores, 3, .3).indices;
  const auto overlap = n::box_iou(d.boxes, d.boxes);
  if (fast.to_vector<int>() != std::vector<int>{0} ||
      greedy.to_vector<int>() != std::vector<int>{0, 2})
    return 1;
  auto p = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(overlap, {0}), 0, 1);
  p.title("Three-box suppression chain");
  p.size(750, 600);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.save_svg("build/yolact_fast_nms.svg");
  std::print("IoU(A,B) {:.6f},IoU(B,C) {:.6f},IoU(A,C) {:.6f};Fast NMS keeps A,greedy NMS "
             "keeps A,C. Diagonal one;shared heatmap range[0,1].\n",
             overlap.to_vector<float>()[1], overlap.to_vector<float>()[5],
             overlap.to_vector<float>()[2]);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
IoU(A,B) 0.428571,IoU(B,C) 0.428571,IoU(A,C) 0.111111;Fast NMS keeps A,greedy NMS keeps A,C. Diagonal one;shared heatmap range[0,1].
\image(figures/yolact_fast_nms.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All pairwise overlaps of three boxes in score order A,B,C,with row zero at the bottom. Fast NMS includes every earlier row in its suppression maximum;only the upper score triangle is relevant.)
