> Full branches,compact fitting dimensions and explicit adaptations

The full model has a ResNet101 backbone,256-channel FPN/shared prediction
feature,32 ReLU prototypes,tanh coefficients and a semantic auxiliary head.
All348 learned parameter gradients execute at64px below;the550px geometry
has69/35/18/9/5 prediction sides,19248 priors and138px prototype maps. The
64px execution is an initialized full-width graph check,not550px training or
pretrained COCO evaluation. The compact model uses ResNet18/divisor8,FPN32,
eight prototypes and ten digit classes. Its five grid sides are8/4/2/1/1,
258 anchors and16px prototypes;every branch remains active.

Background is the **last** class here. Anchors use true aspect ratios1,.5,2,
rather than the original release's legacy square-anchor bug. Crops use discrete
pixel centres,no one-pixel expansion,and at most32 positive masks/image.
Semantic BCE trains the class-specific support union. Tensor shuffles change
the old std::mt19937 positive-mask draw sequence. These source teaching choices
are documented rather than attributed to an exact released training recipe.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool full : {true, false}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
    m::YolactConfig c;
    c.size = 64;
    if (!full) {
      c.classes = 10;
      c.depth = 18;
      c.divisor = 8;
      c.width = 32;
      c.prototypes = 8;
      c.grayscale = true;
    }
    const int channels = full ? 3 : 1;
    const auto images =
        n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 2 * 64 * 64 * channels)).reshape({2, 64, 64, channels});
    const auto net = m::Yolact(p, state, images, c, true);
    auto loss = n::mean(n::square(net.logits));
    for (const auto &v : {net.deltas, net.coefficients, net.prototypes, net.semantic})
      loss = loss + n::mean(n::square(v));
    const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, p.parameters());
    for (const auto &g : gradient)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(g.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()) ||
          (!full && n::sum(n::square(g)).item() <= 0))
        return 1;
    if (full && gradient.size() != 348)
      return 1;
    std::print("{} YOLACT:{} learned/{} BN state scalars,{} finite gradients,{} anchors,{}px "
               "prototype grid at64px.\n",
               full ? "Full" : "Compact", p.count(), state.count(), gradient.size(),
               net.anchors, net.proto_side);
  }
  const auto cells = m::YolactCells(550);
  int anchors = 0;
  for (const auto side : cells)
    anchors += 3 * side * side;
  if (anchors != 19248 || cells != std::vector<int>{69, 35, 18, 9, 5})
    return 1;
  std::print("Full550px geometry19248 priors/138px prototypes checked from five-level grid "
             "formula;full forward/backward executes at64px.\n");
}
```
