> Actual image/support pairs and visible whole-model Adam

Training-source MNIST supplies the first2048 digits for64 fitting and16
validation scenes(seed11),while test-source MNIST supplies first512 digits
for eight test scenes(seed22). Nonoverlapping tight boxes simplify the task;
resampled byte>32 defines each object's individual support. Data/palette and
splits match the documented instance-scene API. The first four fitting pairs
are shown below;no held-out target contributes to optimization.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/yolact_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto digits = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  m::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  cfg.max_overlap = 0;
  const auto scenes = m::MakeTensorInstanceScenes(
      n::slice_axis(digits.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(digits.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(m::InstanceMaskPreview(scenes), "build/yolact_data.png", 1, 0, 1, 4, 1.,
                     3);
  std::print(
      "80 actual64px MNIST training-source scenes:rows0..63 fit,64..79 validation;first four "
      "image/truth-support pairs shown. Up to four attempted digits,nonoverlapping tight "
      "boxes;support is resampled byte>32. Validation never supplies optimization targets.\n");
}
```
