\caption(Complete compact YOLACT optimization with all-branch objectives and paired learned/BN validation selection. The weighted mask contribution is shown separately from the joint loss.)
\alttext(Complete compact YOLACT optimization with all-branch objectives and paired learned/BN validation selection. The weighted mask contribution is shown separately from the joint loss.)

The selected epoch18 has validation box AP50.038677,but all held-out box
and mask AP metrics are zero on26 digits. This run does not learn a useful
held-out detector. The prototype gallery shows learned activations,which by
themselves do not establish successful instance separation. The original
bounded quick executable likewise reports finite diagnostics without enforcing
a convergence claim;its explicit full workflow retains the learning gate.

\image(figures/yolact_predictions.png)
\caption(First four actual held-out image/truth/prediction triples,using the same digit palette. Higher scores overlay lower-scored masks;missed,extra and wrong-class instances remain.)
\alttext(Held-out MNIST images with true individual supports and actual restored YOLACT masks.)
\image(figures/yolact_prototypes.png)
\caption(The first held-out image's eight learned ReLU prototype maps,in channel order left-to-right then top-to-bottom. Native16px maps are nearest-expanded64px;all share the printed[0,maximum] range. They are basis activations,not truth masks or class probabilities.)
\alttext(Eight actual restored shared prototype activation maps,using one common grayscale scale.)

> Conclusion

Exact linear-mask/crop derivatives and suppression-chain fixtures precede initialized full-model checks and complete compact fitting. Explicit targets,all-branch Adam,paired BN restoration and real mask/prototype galleries expose both the mechanism and errors without asserting released COCO accuracy or CPU real-time performance.

> References

- [Bolya,Zhou,Xiao and Lee(2019),YOLACT: Real-time Instance Segmentation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.02689).
- [Authors’ model implementation](https://github.com/dbolya/yolact/blob/master/yolact.py).
